: "a sensitivity analysis restricted the sample to very light (0.00) vs very dark (1.00) players", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["sensitivity analysis"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 114, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[146, 146]], "assertion": "the restricted extreme-tone sample had N=40,992 dyads", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["sample size"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 115, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[147, 147]], "assertion": "the adjusted risk difference in the extreme-tone comparison was 0.27 pp (95% CI -0.11 to 0.65, p=0.164)", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["adjusted risk difference"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 116, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[148, 148]], "assertion": "this extreme-tone finding was consistent with the primary analysis (null result, wider CI due to smaller sample)", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["sensitivity analysis"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 117, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[149, 149]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 118, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[150, 150]], "note": "5.2 subheading"}, {"id": 119, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[151, 151]], "assertion": "unadjusted risk differences were examined separately by league", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["league"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 120, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[152, 152]], "assertion": "England's unadjusted RD was +0.37 pp (dark higher)", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["England"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 121, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[153, 153]], "assertion": "France's unadjusted RD was -0.46 pp (light higher)", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["France"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 122, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[154, 154]], "assertion": "Germany's unadjusted RD was +0.67 pp (dark higher)", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["Germany"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 123, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[155, 155]], "assertion": "Spain's unadjusted RD was -0.42 pp (light higher)", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["Spain"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 124, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[156, 156]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 125, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[157, 157]], "assertion": "there was no consistent pattern across leagues; the overall small positive effect was driven by England/Germany but contradicted by France/Spain, indicating the effect is not robust across contexts", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["league heterogeneity"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 126, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[158, 158]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 127, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[159, 159]], "note": "5.3 subheading"}, {"id": 128, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[160, 160]], "assertion": "unadjusted risk differences were examined separately by position", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["position"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 129, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[161, 161]], "assertion": "Defender unadjusted RD was +0.15 pp", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["defender"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 130, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[162, 162]], "assertion": "Forward unadjusted RD was +0.12 pp", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["forward"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 131, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "other", "lines": [[163, 163]], "note": "line is truncated mid-word ('- **Midf'), apparently the start of a Midfielder position statistic cut off by the report truncation; no interpretable assertion recoverable"}, {"id": 132, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[164, 164]], "assertion": "the hypothesis is not supported", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["hypothesis"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 133, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[165, 165]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 134, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[166, 166]], "assertion": "the adjusted risk difference was 0.18 percentage points (95% CI -0.06 to 0.42, p=0.148)", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["adjusted risk difference"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": [135]}, {"id": 135, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[166, 166]], "assertion": "this result is not statistically significant at alpha=0.05, with the CI including zero, compatible with no effect or a small protective effect", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["adjusted risk difference"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": [134]}, {"id": 136, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[167, 167]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 137, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[168, 168]], "assertion": "the adjusted odds ratio was 1.151 (95% CI 0.956 to 1.386, p=0.138), also not statistically significant", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["adjusted odds ratio"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 138, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[169, 169]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 139, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[170, 170]], "assertion": "the effect at the point estimate (0.18 pp) is quite small", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["effect magnitude"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": [140, 141]}, {"id": 140, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[170, 170]], "assertion": "the median number of referee encounters per player in the dataset is 80", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["referee encounters"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": [139, 141]}, {"id": 141, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[170, 170]], "assertion": "the estimated effect translates to an absolute risk increase of approximately 1 in 556 additional red cards for dark-skinned vs light-skinned players", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["absolute risk increase"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": [139, 140]}, {"id": 142, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[171, 171]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 143, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[172, 172]], "assertion": "the point estimate is in the hypothesized direction and the unadjusted and adjusted estimates are consistent with each other", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["direction of evidence"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": [144]}, {"id": 144, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[172, 172]], "assertion": "the lack of significance and CI including zero mean the null hypothesis of no difference cannot be ruled out", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["null hypothesis"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": [143]}, {"id": 145, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[173, 173]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 146, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[174, 174]], "assertion": "the evidence is inconclusive", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["evidential strength"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": [147]}, {"id": 147, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[174, 174]], "assertion": "a larger sample or more red card events would be needed to detect an effect of this magnitude with adequate power", "polarity": "would_have", "targets": ["statistical power", "sample size"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": [146]}, {"id": 148, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[175, 177]], "note": "blank/divider/blank"}, {"id": 149, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[178, 179]], "note": "section 7 heading"}, {"id": 150, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[180, 180]], "note": "7.1 subheading"}, {"id": 151, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "hedging", "lines": [[181, 181]], "note": "caveat that skin-tone rating, despite high agreement, is inherently subjective and may introduce measurement error"}, {"id": 152, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "hedging", "lines": [[182, 182]], "note": "caveat that photo lighting/quality/angle could affect perceived skin tone"}, {"id": 153, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[183, 183]], "assertion": "the middle skin-tone category was excluded to partially address concerns about reduced power and threshold effects from dichotomizing a continuous measure", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["dichotomization", "middle skin tone"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 154, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[184, 184]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 155, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[185, 185]], "note": "7.2 subheading"}, {"id": 156, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[186, 186]], "assertion": "red cards occurred in only 1.25% of dyads, a rare event rate that reduces statistical power and estimate precision", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["red card rate"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 157, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[187, 187]], "assertion": "the outcome analyzed was binary (whether a dyad ever had a red card), not a count of red cards", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["outcome definition"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": [158]}, {"id": 158, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[187, 187]], "assertion": "a count-based red-card outcome was not used, which may miss dose-response relationships", "polarity": "did_not", "targets": ["outcome definition"], "confidence": "medium", "shares_lines_with": [157]}, {"id": 159, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[188, 188]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 160, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[189, 189]], "note": "7.3 subheading"}, {"id": 161, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "hedging", "lines": [[190, 190]], "note": "caveat that despite adjusting for position, physique, games, goals, and league, other unmeasured factors could still confound results"}, {"id": 162, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[191, 191]], "assertion": "the analysis lacked direct measures of player aggression or foul rate", "polarity": "did_not", "targets": ["play style", "aggression"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 163, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[192, 192]], "assertion": "the analysis did not account for referees potentially responding to a player's prior disciplinary record (reputation effects)", "polarity": "did_not", "targets": ["reputation effects"], "confidence": "medium", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 164, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[193, 193]], "assertion": "the analysis did not account for team-level tactics/aggressiveness", "polarity": "did_not", "targets": ["team tactics"], "confidence": "medium", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 165, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[194, 194]], "assertion": "the analysis lacked referee-level measures of bias", "polarity": "did_not", "targets": ["referee bias"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": [166]}, {"id": 166, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[194, 194]], "assertion": "country-level IAT/explicit bias scores were available but were not used in the primary analysis", "polarity": "did_not", "targets": ["IAT bias scores"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": [165]}, {"id": 167, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[195, 195]], "assertion": "dark-skinned players were underrepresented in certain positions (e.g., goalkeepers=2%) and leagues (e.g., Germany=18%), which could limit comparability", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["positivity assumption"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 168, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[196, 196]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 169, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[197, 197]], "note": "7.4 subheading"}, {"id": 170, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "hedging", "lines": [[198, 198]], "note": "caveat that if missingness in skin-tone data were related to both skin tone and red-card risk, results could be biased"}, {"id": 171, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[199, 199]], "assertion": "players with longer careers (more dyads) are overrepresented in the sample, raising a possible collider/survival bias if skin tone affects career length", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["survival bias"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 172, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[200, 200]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 173, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[201, 201]], "note": "7.5 subheading"}, {"id": 174, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[202, 202]], "assertion": "multiple exploratory sensitivity analyses were conducted (by league, position, etc.)", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["sensitivity analyses"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": [175]}, {"id": 175, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[202, 202]], "assertion": "these exploratory analyses were not adjusted for multiple testing, so some subgroup findings may be false positives", "polarity": "did_not", "targets": ["multiple testing correction"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": [174]}, {"id": 176, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[203, 203]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 177, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[204, 204]], "note": "7.6 subheading"}, {"id": 178, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "hedging", "lines": [[205, 205]], "note": "caveat that findings, limited to four European leagues in one season, may not generalize to other leagues, eras, or sports"}, {"id": 179, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "hedging", "lines": [[206, 206]], "note": "caveat that the binary light/dark categorization may not capture the full spectrum of skin tone or how race operates in real-world referee decisions"}, {"id": 180, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[207, 207]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 181, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[208, 208]], "note": "7.7 subheading"}, {"id": 182, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[209, 209]], "assertion": "the linear probability model did not produce predicted probabilities outside [0,1] in this data", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["linear probability model"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 183, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[210, 210]], "assertion": "1,339 clusters was judged adequate for the large-cluster asymptotics assumption underlying the cluster-robust standard errors", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["cluster-robust standard errors"], "confidence": "medium", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 184, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[211, 211]], "assertion": "the main model assumed the skin-tone effect is constant across covariates (no effect modification)", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["effect modification"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": [185]}, {"id": 185, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[211, 211]], "assertion": "sensitivity analyses suggest heterogeneity by league, which violates the no-effect-modification assumption", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["effect modification", "league"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": [184]}, {"id": 186, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[212, 214]], "note": "blank/divider/blank"}, {"id": 187, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[215, 216]], "note": "section 8 heading"}, {"id": 188, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[217, 217]], "note": "8.1 subheading"}, {"id": 189, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "hedging", "lines": [[218, 218]], "note": "caveat that a lack of significant effect does not prove absence of bias, only failure to detect it in this dataset"}, {"id": 190, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "hedging", "lines": [[219, 219]], "note": "speculation that a true null effect could explain the lack of detected bias given limited sample size"}, {"id": 191, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[220, 220]], "assertion": "a post-hoc power calculation suggests approximately 30% power to detect the ~0.2 pp effect at alpha=0.05", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["statistical power"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 192, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "hedging", "lines": [[221, 221]], "note": "speculation that context-dependent bias in opposite directions across leagues could cancel out in the aggregate estimate"}, {"id": 193, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[222, 222]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 194, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[223, 223]], "note": "8.2 subheading"}, {"id": 195, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "hedging", "lines": [[224, 224]], "note": "caveat about policy implications given statistical insignificance"}, {"id": 196, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[225, 225]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 197, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[226, 226]], "note": "8.3 subheading"}, {"id": 198, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "framing", "lines": [[227, 230]], "note": "suggestions for future research (larger samples, referee-level analysis, experimental methods, mediation analysis)"}, {"id": 199, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[231, 233]], "note": "blank/divider/blank"}, {"id": 200, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[234, 235]], "note": "Reproducibility Statement heading"}, {"id": 201, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[236, 236]], "assertion": "all analyses were conducted using Python 3.11", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["software"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 202, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[237, 243]], "assertion": "specific package versions were used: pandas 2.x, numpy 1.x, statsmodels 0.14, scipy 1.x, scikit-learn 1.x, matplotlib 3.x, seaborn 0.12", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["software packages"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 203, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[244, 244]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 204, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[245, 245]], "assertion": "the complete analysis code was provided in final_analysis.py", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["analysis code"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 205, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[246, 247]], "note": "procedural reproduction instructions (place file, run script)"}, {"id": 206, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[248, 248]], "assertion": "the code output includes full regression tables and a 4-panel figure (soccer_analysis.png)", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["output", "figure"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 207, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[249, 249]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 208, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "background", "lines": [[250, 250]], "note": "dataset provenance: 2,053 players, 3,147 referees, skin tone coded by two raters, red cards from a sports statistics company"}, {"id": 209, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[251, 251]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 210, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[252, 252]], "assertion": "the submitted code is fully reproducible and documented", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["analysis code"], "confidence": "medium", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 211, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[253, 253]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 212, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[254, 254]], "assertion": "the analysis was not pre-registered", "polarity": "did_not", "targets": ["pre-registration"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": [213, 214]}, {"id": 213, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[254, 254]], "assertion": "analytic choices (covariates, exclusions, skin tone cutoffs) were made based on data exploration and substantive reasoning", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["analytic choices"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": [212, 214]}, {"id": 214, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[254, 254]], "assertion": "analytic choices were not made in order to achieve a particular result", "polarity": "did_not", "targets": ["analytic choices"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": [212, 213]}, {"id": 215, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[255, 257]], "note": "blank/divider/blank"}, {"id": 216, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[258, 259]], "note": "Final Answer heading"}, {"id": 217, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "framing", "lines": [[260, 260]], "note": "restated hypothesis"}, {"id": 218, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[261, 261]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 219, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[262, 262]], "assertion": "the conclusion is that the hypothesis is NOT SUPPORTED", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["hypothesis"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 220, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[263, 263]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 221, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[264, 264]], "assertion": "the adjusted risk difference of 0.18 pp (95% CI -0.06 to 0.42, p=0.148) is not statistically significant, with the point estimate in the hypothesized direction but the CI including zero and p exceeding 0.05", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["adjusted risk difference"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": [222, 223]}, {"id": 222, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[264, 264]], "assertion": "the evidence is insufficient to conclude dark-skinned players face systematically higher red-card risk after adjustment", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["conclusion"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": [221, 223]}, {"id": 223, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[264, 264]], "assertion": "key limitations are low power from rare events, possible unmeasured confounding, and heterogeneity across leagues", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["limitations"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": [221, 222]}, {"id": 224, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[265, 265]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 225, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[266, 266]], "note": "tool-output closing tag"}]}}